Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:03.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What if every human had a clone that hated them?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.30,0:00:04.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You walk past a mirror.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.70,0:00:06.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your reflection doesn't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.50,0:00:07.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It's you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.20,0:00:09.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But it's staring at you with pure hate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.80,0:00:10.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.50,0:00:12.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}That's over eight billion clones.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.80,0:00:18.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In 1996, Dolly the sheep became the first mammal cloned from an adult cell.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.30,0:00:21.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It took two hundred seventy-seven tries.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.00,0:00:25.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your clone would share your DNA… but not a single one of your memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.30,0:00:26.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It would start life as a baby.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.90,0:00:32.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Even identical twins, nature's own clones, have different fingerprints.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.30,0:00:33.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Eight billion people.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.70,0:00:36.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Each hunted by their own face.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.20,0:00:37.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.50,0:00:39.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your clone could never truly be you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.60,0:00:42.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It doesn't know your fears or your secrets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.20,0:00:45.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Only one person does… you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.20,0:00:46.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.20,0:00:48.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your worst enemy was never a copy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.70,0:00:51.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Would you want to meet your clone?
